<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_TarShallow_GeneratedFilth.xml   UtinniPatches — SUMP_WALKWAYS_1

  Wires vanilla's own foot-tracking mechanism onto RM_TarShallow: a pawn
  standing in shallow tar picks up RM_Filth_Tar "on its boots"
  (Pawn_FilthTracker.TryPickupFilth, RimWorld/Pawn_FilthTracker.cs — reads
  TerrainDef.generatedFilth directly, Source/Verse/TerrainDef.cs:292) and
  later tracks it onto the next dry floor it crosses
  (Pawn_FilthTracker.Notify_EnteredNewCell/TryDropFilth) — the SAME real
  engine mechanism vanilla uses for e.g. Sand terrain tracking Filth_Sand
  indoors. This is duckboards' own "fouls with tar" half (item spec §1);
  RM_Filth_Tar.xml (FlowWorks) carries the actual movement penalty via its
  own pathCost, see that file's header.

  Kept as its OWN file, separate from RUT_TarShallow_FilthAcceptance.xml
  (SUMP_MECHANICS_1 S4, already shipped/undheld) that this op DEPENDS on
  (TerrainDef.ConfigErrors requires filthAcceptanceMask & Terrain wherever
  generatedFilth is set, TerrainDef.cs:538 — that sibling file's own
  Operation already satisfies it) — so that THIS file's own DEPLOY_HOLD
  (below) never touches the already-working mouse-track fix.

  DEPLOY_HOLD LIFTED, SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1 (2026-09-24): RM_Filth_Tar now
  ships placeholder art (three blob sprites, that def's own header) and is
  deployed, so <generatedFilth> — a direct ThingDef reference the config
  loader resolves by name, same class of reference the cross-mod xref system
  resolves at load — no longer dangles. Lifted in the same pass as
  RM_Filth_Tar.xml's own hold, per that entry's own instruction.

  No MayRequire/FindMod gate — same posture as the sibling
  filthAcceptanceMask fix this depends on (that file's own header explains
  why: every other Sump-side reference to RM_TarShallow already assumes it
  is a live, always-loaded dependency).
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/TerrainDef[defName="RM_TarShallow"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <generatedFilth>RM_Filth_Tar</generatedFilth>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
